{"availability":"available","full":"pierrebrunelle/pixeltable-mural-registry","name":"pixeltable-mural-registry","description":"Public-art mural registry API: wall photo uploads with thumbnails, grayscale copies and color tags · built with Pixeltable","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T22:54:44Z","updated":"2026-10-08T06:36:27Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pierrebrunelle.github.io/awesome-pixeltable-apps/#pixeltable-mural-registry","topics":["computer-vision","concurrency","fastapi","image-processing","multimodal","pixeltable","pixeltable-example","python","street-art","udf"],"demo":"https://pierrebrunelle.github.io/awesome-pixeltable-apps/#pixeltable-mural-registry","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:56.858Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:56.858Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T06:39:56.858Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T06:39:56.858Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A registry of a city's murals. Upload a wall photo with the title, artist and neighborhood, and Pixeltable stores the image, then derives a 96x64 thumbnail and a grayscale copy as media computed columns. A chain of PIL-based UDFs tags the aspect ratio, the dominant color channel and an overall tone. The API accepts multipart uploads (in parallel), lists murals by neighborhood, runs the analysis on an upload without storing it, and serves a mural's thumbnail as an image file.","Pixeltable is open-source, Python-native multimodal AI data infrastructure: tables, incremental computed columns, UDFs, indexes and serving in one library, running locally or on Pixeltable Cloud.","⭐ Like this example? Star pixeltable/pixeltable on GitHub. It helps other developers find it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pierrebrunelle/pixeltable-mural-registry/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"dde5cc6dfcf2ce028ffffc1468